00:17:02,360 --> 00:17:04,360
And you also need to rehearse

302
00:17:04,360 --> 00:17:06,360
how you're going to lead that practice.

303
00:17:06,360 --> 00:17:08,360
So that's what a patrol leader does.

304
00:17:08,360 --> 00:17:10,360
It's pretty simple,

305
00:17:10,360 --> 00:17:12,360
And then I'm going to go over the entire thing again.

306
00:17:12,360 --> 00:17:14,360
What's your goal?

307
00:17:14,360 --> 00:17:16,360
To lead, train and inspire Scouts

308
00:17:16,360 --> 00:17:18,360
to become first class.

309
00:17:18,360 --> 00:17:20,360
How do Scouts become first class?

310
00:17:20,360 --> 00:17:22,360
By doing the things that Scouts do.

311
00:17:22,360 --> 00:17:24,360
What do Scouts do?

312
00:17:24,360 --> 00:17:26,360
They apply them to their activities,

313
00:17:26,360 --> 00:17:28,360
They explore hobbies and careers,

314
00:17:28,360 --> 00:17:30,360
They serve their community

315
00:17:30,360 --> 00:17:32,360
And they're responsible to organize

316
00:17:32,360 --> 00:17:34,360
and plan their activities

317
00:17:34,360 --> 00:17:36,360
as they put the Scout Oath

318
00:17:36,360 --> 00:17:38,360
and Law into practice.

319
00:17:38,360 --> 00:17:40,360
So how is it that Scouts do these things?

