00:18:28,360 --> 00:18:30,360
lots of other opportunities to expand

345
00:18:30,360 --> 00:18:32,360
on the complexities of all this,

346
00:18:32,360 --> 00:18:34,360
But if the patrol leaders have this simple

347
00:18:34,360 --> 00:18:36,360
catechism in their minds,

348
00:18:36,360 --> 00:18:38,360
they get a really good overview of everything.

349
00:18:38,360 --> 00:18:40,360
and I can explain the specifics

350
00:18:40,360 --> 00:18:42,360
by asking them the applicable question.

351
00:18:42,360 --> 00:18:44,360
That's why it's important

352
00:18:44,360 --> 00:18:46,360
that we all know

353
00:18:46,360 --> 00:18:48,360
the questions and answers.

354
00:18:48,360 --> 00:18:50,360
So, as an example of this,

355
00:18:50,360 --> 00:18:52,360
suppose we're observing

356
00:18:52,360 --> 00:18:54,360
a patrol leaders council before

357
00:18:54,360 --> 00:18:56,360
a regular troop meeting

358
00:18:56,360 --> 00:18:58,360
and they're just milling around

359
00:18:58,360 --> 00:19:00,360
and they're not doing much of anything.

360
00:19:00,360 --> 00:19:02,360
and so I pull the senior patrol leader aside

361
00:19:02,360 --> 00:19:04,360
and I ask: what are the three steps

362
00:19:04,360 --> 00:19:06,360
to making things happen?

363
00:19:06,360 --> 00:19:08,360
Well, hopefully by this time,

364
00:19:08,360 --> 00:19:10,360
by repetition, he knows

365
00:19:10,360 --> 00:19:12,360
planning, preparation and execution.

366
00:19:12,360 --> 00:19:14,360
and I ask: what step

367
00:19:14,360 --> 00:19:16,360
are you in right now?

368
00:19:16,360 --> 00:19:18,360
What applies to me?

369
00:19:18,360 --> 00:19:20,360
Well, I think we're in preparation.

370
00:19:20,360 --> 00:19:22,360
and I ask: so everything is prepared.

371
00:19:22,360 --> 00:19:24,360
you can start the meeting right now.

372
00:19:24,360 --> 00:19:26,360
you have all the stuff that you need.

373
00:19:26,360 --> 00:19:28,360
everybody's ready to go.

374
00:19:28,360 --> 00:19:30,360
and he looks at me and he says

375
00:19:30,360 --> 00:19:32,360
something like: well, I guess so.

376
00:19:32,360 --> 00:19:34,360
and I say: well,

377
00:19:34,360 --> 00:19:36,360
what do you need to do to answer

378
00:19:36,360 --> 00:19:38,360
that question a little more. certainly,

379
00:19:38,360 --> 00:19:40,360
And most of the time he'll get the idea

380
00:19:40,360 --> 00:19:42,360
and he will motivate everybody

381
00:19:42,360 --> 00:19:44,360
to get in that preparation mode

382
00:19:44,360 --> 00:19:46,360
and around waiting for things to happen.

383
00:19:46,360 --> 00:19:48,360
Now, because we have this shared understanding

384
00:19:48,360 --> 00:19:50,360
and a rote memory of these things,

385
00:19:50,360 --> 00:19:52,360
I can do things like that. I can coach

386
00:19:52,360 --> 00:19:54,360
a patrol leader or the senior patrol leader

387
00:19:54,360 --> 00:19:56,360
or any of the youth leadership in a few seconds

388
00:19:56,360 --> 00:19:58,360
and they feel confident

